{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:14Z","created_by_operation":"op_18a87f86df854f609ead26b3a04c36dd","id":"pg_8ad0577f6e6e5e3ebc1cf2398fa5f170","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/orionstarai-easycode-docs-tools-memory-md-887b8bb4b5a8-f2398fa5f170.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_e50658a3dbf65801bdb57f9b96618e43"],"title":"OrionStarAI/EasyCode/docs/tools/memory.md @ 887b8bb4b5a8","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:14Z","updated_by_operation":"op_18a87f86df854f609ead26b3a04c36dd"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_092f123927b7cfb9727fdd1cdab77ee6dc3865665412f6acb13b3368d1f290f6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Built-in tools include file operations (read_file, write_file, replace, delete_file), search (glob, grep via ripgrep), shell execution, web_fetch/web_search, task sub-agent, todo_write, and memory."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1af3e42696c05fccdfa99268a4af63ac2972d7171715e003f77280383261a0a3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is a monorepo with a CLI package (React Ink terminal UI, commands, services, auth) and a core package containing tools, MCP engine, prompts, hooks, skills, and config modules."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1ee1daa61620bc82731565db57c7be45f1416011a633a7ca0609e6b5f8d7019c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Delegated external-agent sessions can be resumed with a resume sub-syntax that reloads full session history via session/load, and task records persist under ~/.easycode-user/delegate-tasks/."},{"claim_ids":["clm_258ef96da80b6c6352ae080d1315060b07eee0b08004d7ca55ab874dc27c5ab1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MCP servers can be configured in .easycode/settings.json either as local processes (command/args/env) or via Streamable HTTP endpoints with headers, including trust and include/exclude tool options."},{"claim_ids":["clm_29b4858e0d0eefae73f70f7a4467bbc382696be3d86309f2db4f95709bd2d1f0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Interactive mode provides slash commands including /help, /session, /model, /compress, /tools, /mcp, /memory, /plan, /yolo, /restore, /theme, /auth, and /init."},{"claim_ids":["clm_32d45750f01cadabf9ea7caaae1c3930e0d65ec8fc22ebb1740590a643003c44"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The stack uses TypeScript 5.x on Node.js 20+, React+Ink for CLI UI, esbuild for building, Vitest for tests, @google/genai for Gemini, and @modelcontextprotocol/sdk for MCP."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4901f1c505d637f4e6956a7eebaac6b49bfa0e796543717cffe2b4343c7512bb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Custom models can be configured in OpenAI-compatible or Anthropic Claude formats via a /model management wizard or ~/.easycode-user/custom-models.json, with fields like provider, baseUrl, apiKey, modelId, and optional enableThinking."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6221f6421c04067d701ebafb07996313accfc5149883d434fb72831811e7c143"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors clone the repo, run npm install, build with npm run build, test with npm run test, and run lint and typecheck before committing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6e375d19dfd95015fbd811ba9fbe2e5b8ac87a5e1e9b3d1039c0ae6103bd16a1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tools carry documented safety levels: read-only tools like read_file and grep, confirmation-required tools like write_file, replace, and shell, with a --yolo mode that auto-executes all operations without confirmation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_95beccbc791540fd0fd9123255ef231bbb859a3247c8e507291cbfa0f411dfda"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product is a CLI launched with the `easycode` command, supporting options such as --model, --prompt, --sandbox, --yolo, --continue, --session, --workdir, and --list-sessions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b0a4759fd6bd63a9976c8ef484059174c72692dfa690240cf4a38292bf2a79cd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Easy Code can act as an ACP orchestrator, delegating coding tasks to locally installed Claude Code or Codex via pinned ACP bridge packages, triggered by the model, @cc/@codex prefixes, or /bind in Feishu."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cb44563caa89b28ec5cac1985238874c07d3b6bbd8320994de254b5ef691effb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions are persisted with automatic history saving, resumable via --continue or --session, with history compression to save tokens and checkpoint-based file rollback via /restore."}],"claim_ids":["clm_092f123927b7cfb9727fdd1cdab77ee6dc3865665412f6acb13b3368d1f290f6","clm_1af3e42696c05fccdfa99268a4af63ac2972d7171715e003f77280383261a0a3","clm_1ee1daa61620bc82731565db57c7be45f1416011a633a7ca06